zoe (PM): quick thread: need a pragmatic spec for admission + fallback behavior for reserved pools. goal: predictable outcomes, clear customer messaging, and safe rollout.

zoe (PM): proposal in one line: tiny rule-set evaluated in the routing layer (cached flags) -> outputs: ADMIT, QUEUE, FALLBACK, PREEMPTABLE. include machine reason codes.

rahul (Eng-Platform): agree. keep runtime cheap: cache per-tenant 8-bit flags + small ints (burn_score, committed_ratio) in routing with 3-10s TTL. avoid DB on hot path.

mei (SRE): please add safety controls: per-pool preempt budget, donor protection (dont steal if donor p95 cpu>75%), and automatic conservative mode when pool p99 spikes.

jamal (Customer Success): customers expect two things: (1) opt-in "hard_guarantee" for ultra critical workloads; (2) clear Console copy + a machine reason code so they can automate alerts.

rahul (Eng-Platform): sketch of evaluator below. plan to implement as a tiny state machine in routing layer.

```
// cached per-tenant: flags(mask), burn_score(int), committed_ratio(int)
// cached per-pool: available, preempt_budget
if (flags & HARD_GUARANTEE) {
  if (pool.available >= req.size) return ADMIT("hard_guarantee")
  else return QUEUE("hard_guarantee_no_capacity")
}
if (flags & SOFT_GUARANTEE) {
  if (pool.can_spare_short()) return ADMIT("soft_guarantee_spare")
  if (pool.preempt_budget>0 && donor_ok()) return ADMIT_PREEMPTABLE("soft_guarantee_preempt")
  return QUEUE("soft_guarantee_wait")
}
// opportunistic
if (burn_score < burn_threshold && committed_ratio > comm_threshold) return ADMIT("opportunistic_committed")
return FALLBACK("opportunistic_fallback")
```

rahul (Eng-Platform): donor_ok() checks donor load + recent error spikes; fast-circuit if donor p99 rose >X% in 1m.

mei (SRE): preempt behavior: bounded by max_preempt_per_minute and per-tenant daily cap. also require cooldown: if pool_preempt_rate triggers alert, disable preempt for N minutes.

jamal (Customer Success): UX: Console should show human text + code. examples: "denied: POOL_FULL (code: pool_full)", "preemptable: GRACE_PREEMPT (code: preemptable_grace)", "fallback: CROSS_REGION (code: fallback_cross_region)". also add tips: "Consider Reserved upgrade or reduce burst window."

zoe (PM): rollout acceptance checklist draft: 1) canary synthetic (3 tenants) shows p99 delta <=5%; 2) no more than 2 preempts/day for alpha tenants; 3) reason codes appear in Console and API; 4) feature flag gated by region; 5) telemetry coverage for preempt rate, fallback rate, queue latency.

sim-bot: scheduled: reserve-admit-sim at 1799999015 to generate spike profiles.

rahul (Eng-Platform): one more tie-breaker: when scores equal prefer higher committed_ratio to discourage burst gaming.

mei (SRE): final ask: add an emergency flip: global_conservative_mode if >Y% of pools hit p99 uplift simultaneously.

zoe (PM): action items: rahul -> prototype routing evaluator + cache; mei -> define concrete thresholds for circuits and preempt budgets; jamal -> prepare Console copy + machine reason code mapping; i'll produce the decision doc and coordinate canary. target: prototype by EOW, canary next week.

jamal (Customer Success): will collect interested enterprise customers for opt-in.

zoe (PM): saving this thread as canonical; will post doc link when ready. :white_check_mark:
